---
/**
 * One weekday row in `ScheduleEditor.astro`: the weekday label and a
 * routine picker. Reads `row`/`index` from the enclosing `x-for` and
 * `routineLabel()`/`routines` from `scheduleEditor()`.
 *
 * A native `<select>` rather than a shared component: no select primitive
 * exists in `components/forms/` (only `Input.astro`), and per the plan this
 * is the accepted exception (`docs/architecture/07-Frontend/08-Component-Inventory.md`).
 * Its "Rest" option's value is `""`; `row.routineTemplateId` is otherwise a
 * real routine id, `null` for a freshly-created rest row — the two falsy
 * shapes are reconciled once, in `schedule-editor.data.ts`'s `payload()`,
 * rather than here.
 */
---

<li class="flex items-center gap-3">
  <span
    class="w-24 shrink-0 text-sm font-semibold text-foreground"
    x-text="weekdayLabel(index)"
  ></span>
  <select
    class="input w-full rounded-md border border-border px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-foreground outline-none transition-[border-color,box-shadow,background-color] duration-150"
    x-model="row.routineTemplateId"
    aria-label="Routine"
  >
    <option value="">Rest</option>
    <template
      x-for="routine in routines"
      :key="routine.routineId"
    >
      <option
        :value="routine.routineId"
        x-text="routineLabel(routine)"
      ></option>
    </template>
  </select>
</li>
